latforming  expectations and with the openness of  banjo kazooie's massive moveset and  magical transformations it's open season  for platonic to innovate but it's not  just the mechanics at play here play  tonics commitment to delivering a  satisfying final product shines forth  and many other manifestations it's been  confirmed that not only will ukulele  make use of that disney-esque dynamic  music theming that made the banjo game  so immersive but the music will also be  composed by rare legend grant kirkhope  of the banjo kazooie fame and the  illustrious david wise the man  responsible for among many other gems  this little  platonic have also stated their  intention to give each character a hyper  detailed backstory complete with  rivalries alliances friends foes and  subjective morality z' that may paint  them as evil in this game but set them  up to be the protagonist in a future  game into that point they're fully  intending some of these characters to  populate future games and not  necessarily only within the 3d  platforming genre the comparison they  made was that this will be a Marvel  Universe level of detail with each  character opening their own world of  possibilities and if there's even a  shred of truth to that that I'm weeping  with excitement over this the worlds  these characters will inhabit are as of  yet a mystery the only pieces of the  various worlds we've seen are in these  still images and a bit of demo footage  from what looks like your basic starter  world jungle level but discovery of new  worlds will be a huge component of the  excitement in any banjo kazooie  spiritual successor remember the first  time you entered gobies desert for mad  monster mansion those moments put me on  the edge of my seat as I tried to guess  what sort of Mambo transformation or new  scale or strange quests and characters  awaited me within each new realm further  platonic has confirmed that these levels  will grow as you progress through the  game ozone will most likely either be a  much larger or a completely different  place when you're finished than when you  began and in traditional banjo-kazooie  form a massive hub world will tie beus  realms together with each new section  unlocked through collection of pages  and/or the skills you'll acquire in each  level as you progress the collectibles  and secrets will also spill over into  the hub world some of them apparently so  well hidden that platonic are claiming  it'll take months or even years for fans  to find you may call me the static or  idealistic in hell I may very well be  but after consuming every bit of  information platonic is released about  ukulele I'm about 10 times as excited as  I was when I began these gentlemen have  promised to keep what people love about  all rare games not over promise anything  and to listen closely to what fans want  from ukulele in order to craft the most  perfect follow-up to the banjo kazooie  games imaginable and i quite frankly  couldn't be more hyped over it Godspeed  platonic games and while you're at it  Conker's Bad Fur Day too would be really  really nice
 

